; (define (incr x) (+ x 1)) (incr 0), with + expanded, as basic blocks: a fixnum fast path with its
; overflow check, a flonum case, a generic fallback. With intervals, ΛV calls incr with x exactly 0, so
; the call returns exactly 1 and has no side effect: with fold=true it is folded (spec 9.5).
function main()
M:  call incr(0) -> N
N:  return #res

function incr(x)
A:  if fixnum?(x) goto B else goto C
B:  r = fx+?(x, 1)
    if r goto R else goto D
R:  return r
C:  if flonum?(x) goto F else goto D
F:  return fl+(x, 1.0)
D:  return ##+(x, 1)
